course: dictionary
lesson: 614
title: Axis, the line things spin on
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An axis is an imaginary straight line that something spins around. «The Earth spins on its axis once a day.» You cannot touch the Earth's axis, because it is only a line we imagine through the middle of the Earth, from the North Pole to the South Pole.
explain: In maths, an axis is one of the main lines on a graph. «The x-axis goes across the graph and the y-axis goes up.» Each axis has a label and a scale, which help you read the numbers.
explain: Look at the words around axis to work out which meaning fits. If the sentence talks about spinning, tilting or poles, think of the imaginary line. If it talks about graphs, labels or coordinates, think of maths. Then swap in the word line and check that the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Axis is a noun with a plural. One axis, two «axes». Words like axes and axis look alike, so check the number of things in the sentence before you choose.
fact: An axis is an imaginary straight line that something spins around.
fact: «The North Pole and the South Pole are the two ends of the Earth's axis.»
fact: «The Earth's axis is tilted by about 23.4 degrees.»
fact: On a graph, the x-axis goes across and the y-axis goes up.
fact: One axis, two axes: «axes» is the plural of axis. An axis of symmetry is a line that cuts a shape into two matching halves.
exercise: «The Earth spins on its axis once a day.» What is an axis? | *An imaginary straight line that something spins around | A kind of graph with numbers | A real rope tied around the Earth | A sort of hot wind
exercise: On a graph, which axis goes up? | The Earth's axis | The x-axis | *The y-axis | The axis of symmetry
exercise: «The maths teacher drew two axes on the board.» Find and copy the plural of axis. | *axes | drew | board | axis
test: «The Earth's axis is tilted, so summer days are long.» What does this tell you about the Earth's axis? | *It is slanted, not straight up and down | It is a line that is bent | It is very short | It is made of metal
test: An axis of symmetry is a line that does what to a shape? | *Cuts it into two matching halves | Measures its weight | Adds a label to it | Makes it spin very fast
exam: «The two ends of the Earth's axis are the North Pole and the South Pole.» Which two things are the ends of the Earth's axis? | The equator and the Sun | Two halves of a shape | *The North Pole and the South Pole | The x-axis and the y-axis
